sion, graduation, and NCLEX outcomes. • Develop and maintain academic support resources, workshops, and online learning materials. • Contribute to continuous quality improvement initiatives supporting student success. Reporting • Track and report data on usage of coaching services, NCLEX pass rate, etc. Teaching and Service Expectations • Participate in faculty meetings, committees, and campus and college student success initiatives. • Engage in professional development related to academic coaching, student success, nursing education, learning science, and NCLEX preparation. Required Qualifications • Master's degree in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution. • Current unencumbered Registered Nurse license or eligibility for licensure in Oklahoma. • Minimum of three years of nursing education, clinical practice, or student support experience. • Demonstrated knowledge of nursing curriculum, NCLEX preparation, and student success strategies. • Strong interpersonal, communication, and mentoring skills. • Experience working with student populations. Preferred Qualifications • Previous teaching experience in a prelicensure nursing program. • Experience with academic coaching, tutoring, remediation, or student success programs. • Knowledge of accessibility practices and support for students with accommodations. • Experience using learning analytics and student performance data to support academic success. • Certification or training in coaching, mentoring, learning strategies, or NCLEX preparation. Required Skills and Background • A strong and demonstrated commitment to integrating the clinical mission in the academy. • Proven ability to provide leadership in a complex environment. • Demonstrated leadership and effectiveness in building strong working relationships with a collaborative style. • Enjoy interacting with people and ability to easily connect with faculty and staff in the College and University across disciplines and among external entities in the community. • Evidence of successful collaborations with community partners and faculty teams in an academic setting; effective communication skills; knowledge of nursing academic curricula and programs; ability to plan and conduct effective meetings; and leadership ability. • Demonstrated ability to be engaging and persuasive with strong teamwork skills; politically astute, diplomatic, and able to manage by influence. • Flexible and capable of responding to multiple demands in a time-sensitive manner. • Ability to exercise astute judgment in all matters related to academic affairs. • Proficient with MS Office applications, learning management software, and other technology used in teaching, research, and practice. To apply, please submit letter of interest, CV, and three professional references. To inquire about the application process, please contact Nursing-HR@ouhsc.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189873": {
      "title": "Assistant - Associate - Professor, Chair of Population Health and Health Systems Sciences Department, College of Nursing",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Nursing Location: Oklahoma City, OK  Purpose of Role: The Department Chair assists the Dean in overseeing College of Nursing faculty in order to meet the tripartite mission of the college including teaching, research and creative/scholarly activity and professional and University service and public outreach.  The Department Chair is responsible for oversight of promotion processes, faculty development programs, faculty recruitment and retention, faculty evaluation, faculty personnel actions, faculty governance, and initiatives pertaining to the faculty well-being for all campus sites. The Department Chair is a key member of the Dean’s leadership team and will provide strategic insight and assist the Dean in setting college goals. The Department Chair will also foster and maintain positive relationships with College and University leadership and community stakeholders including OUH and clinical site partners. Critical to the Chairperson’s success will be their ability to develop and articulate a clear vision and strategy for the department that aligns with the University of Oklahoma’s Lead On, University Strategic Plan. Appointment: This is a full-time, 12-month in-person faculty appointment, Consecutive Term or Tenure-Track eligible, at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor, commensurate with qualifications and experience. This is a 50% administrative position with faculty appointment commensurate with rank and scholarship. Reporting Structure : The Department Chair reports directly to the Dean of the Fran and Earl Ziegler College of Nursing. Responsibilities: 1. Provides leadership in faculty development initiatives that foster faculty career progression 2. Establishes and implements faculty development initiatives for faculty career progression including one-on-one or group-based coaching for identifying mentoring needs and/or creating individualized professional development plans for faculty to address challenges and opportunities of teaching students, engaging in scholarship or research, participating in professional service, and other professional development needs . · Provides guidance to faculty members in role and career development and goal attainment and in seeking promotion and/or tenure . · Participates in course evaluation discussions each semester with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and Academic Program Directors; with the goal of improving academic programs. · Collaborates with the Associate Dean of Research to support programmatic research at the College. · Establishes systems to monitor the impact of faculty development programs and mid-tenure review · Develops mechanisms for recognizing teaching, research/scholarship and service accomplishments of the faculty and coordinates the identification of faculty for training and leadership opportunities. 3. Works with Academic Affairs; the Associate Dean for Research; and the Director of Clinical Affairs, Outreach, and Practice Innovation to create faculty workload plans. · Works with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and Academic Program Directors on teaching assignments. · Works with the Associate Dean for Research on research productivity and scholarship. · Conducts annual faculty evaluations, in collaboration with the Academic Program Directors, Assistant Deans, Associate Deans, and Dean. 4. Oversees the recruitment and hiring of department faculty. Works with leadership to identify priorities in strategic faculty recruitment and works collaboratively in the recruitment process. Oversees and supports the work of faculty search committees. Collaborates with Academic Program Directors in the hiring of adjunct faculty. Oversees the orientation of full-time and adjunct faculty to the goals, policies, and procedures of the College and University. 5. In collaboration with the Assistant Deans, Associate Deans, and Dean , creates and supports an environment that encourages faculty teaching, scholarship, service, and practice. · Maintains ongoing communication with Academic Program Directors and relevant faculty leaders regarding faculty developmental needs in teaching, research, practice, and service. · Formalizes faculty-mentoring process in collaboration with the Faculty Affairs Committee. · Evaluates all faculty to ensure they are prepared academically and experientially for their positions and responsibilities. 6. In collaboration with Academic Program Directors, Assistant Deans, Associate Deans, and Dean, contributes to activities that support faculty work and retention. · Actively contributes to activities related to Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval reviews/reports and all University and national accreditation reviews/reports. · Functions as the executive sponsor, writing support letters for faculty going up for promotion; drawing information from key personnel. · Supports faculty dossier/portfolio preparation for mid-rank review, tenure, and promotion . · Analyzes trends in faculty goal attainment, identifies trends and issues inhibiting faculty success, and proposes action steps to remedy or enhance department faculty development and retention. 7. Manages and ensures successful faculty award and recognition processes including College, University, and State Higher Education Awards, Fellowship in the American Academy of Nursing, National Organization of Nurse Practitioner Faculties, National Association of Clinical Nurse Specialists, Sigma Theta Tau, and other professional society awards. 8. Works collaboratively with the Dean and Associate Deans to develop, implement and evaluate academic programs as they relate to the College’s master plan. 9. Collaborates with Student Affairs and Academic Affairs to ensure the timely response to student complaints, grievances, appeals, and other academic issues per OUHC and College policy and procedures. 10. Represents the College of Nursing on University committees. 11. Participates in teaching, scholarly and clinical activities; and service commensurate with criteria for faculty rank. 12. Serves as a member of the Dean’s Leadership Team. 13. Other Duties as assigned by the Dean. Minimum Qualifications: Licensure: Must be eligible for or hold current registered professional nurse (RN) license for the State of Oklahoma Education: Terminal Degree (Preferably in Nursing or Health Related Field) Experience: · 3 years higher education teaching · 5 years progressive administrative experience · 3 years administrative experience in higher education · A record of scholarship, (extramural funding preferred) · Eligible for appointment at the rank of Assistant, Associate or Professor Required Skills: · Proven ability to provide leadership in a complex environment. · Demonstrated leadership and effectiveness in building strong working relationships with a collaborative style. · Enjoy interacting with people and can easily connect with faculty and staff in the College and University, across disciplines and among external entities in the community. · Evidence of successful collaborations with community partners and faculty teams in an academic setting; effective communication skills; knowledge of nursing academic curricula and programs; ability to plan and conduct effective meetings. · Demonstrated ability to be engaging and persuasive with strong teamwork skills, politically astute, diplomatic, and able to manage by influence. · Demonstrates ability to recruit and retain outstanding faculty, work effectively with leadership,  effectively delegate. · Flexible and capable of responding to multiple demands in a time-sensitive manner. · Ability to exercise astute judgment in all matters related to faculty development activities and monitoring career progression. · Proficient with MS Office applications, learning management software, and other technology used in teaching, research, and practice. To apply, please submit letter of intent, CV, and three professional references to https://apply.interfolio.com/46259/positions . To inquire about the application process, please contact Nursing-HR@ouhsc.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192626": {
      "title": "Instructor - Clinical Assistant - Clinical Associate Professor,  Assistant CRNA Program Director, College of Nursing",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Nursing Location: Oklahoma City, OK  The Assistant Program Director is responsible for the day-to-day operation of the CRNA program in the absence of the Assistant Dean and Program Director. The Assistant Program Director for the CRNA Program supports the student success of the OUHC CON CRNA program across the student life cycle. The assistant program director is a key member in day-to-day operations, promoting a student success model for the OU CON student experience, participating in accreditation processes, providing leadership in the development, implementation and assessment of academic programs and the College and University strategic plans. Appointment : The Assistant Director reports to the Assistant Dean and Program Director for the CRNA program. This position carries approximately 40% administrative release time; release time is negotiated annually with the Dean based on the demands of the role and needs of the OU CON. Responsibilities: Teaching/Learning : Collaborate in the implementation of the OU CON CRNA curricula, ensuring rapid and convenient access to nursing education, electronically or face-to-face. Implement academic and educational policies in collaboration with the Office for Academic Affairs and the Office for Student Affairs. Student Support: Collaborate in the orientation of Student Affairs staff to ensure delivery of advising, tutoring, and special student initiatives within the CRNA program. Cooperate with Department Chairs, Academic Affairs, and Student Affairs to ensure an excellent student experience that prepares graduates to succeed in meeting their life and career goals, consistent with student experience. Operations: Collaborate with CRNA Program Director as well as other Program Directors, Assistant Dean for Student Affairs, Department Chairs, Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, and the Dean to support strategic planning, and information management for the CRNA program; and maintain contracts with outside health care or educational agencies as necessary to ensure appropriate clinical teaching. Monitor nursing education and nursing workforce trends that will impact CON CRNA Program and make recommendations to the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Assistant Dean of Student Affairs, and Dean. University and Campus Relations: Represent faculty and students at college, campus, or University levels related to CRNA Program. Community Relations: Serve as a liaison between OU College of Nursing and CRNA community of interest including CRNAs, anesthesiologists, clinical agencies, and professional groups to promote interests of the OU College of Nursing for mutual benefit. Cooperate in the development and implementation of College of Nursing education, research, and practice marketing plans to enhance the on-campus and off-campus visibility of OU Nursing. Facilitate alumni relations in concert with the OU CON Office for External and Alumni Affairs. Licensure: Eligible for or hold a current registered nurse license and an APRN license in the State of Oklahoma.  Unlicensed faculty may not teach undergraduate and graduate clinical nursing courses. Education: Graduate degree in Nursing and Doctoral degree in Nursing, Health, Science, or Social Science Related Field  is  required. Faculty teaching in the PhD Program must meet the HSC Graduate College faculty appointment guidelines for Associate Member or Full Member Appointment at level 3 or 4 authority. Minimal Experience: Faculty teaching in the nurse anesthesia advanced practice programs must hold appropriate specialty certification Have a minimum of three  years of clinical advanced practice registered nurse experience in the specialty. Preferred Experience: 5 years' experience practicing as a CRNA Academic  experience in curriculum, evaluation, and assessment 2 years’ teaching in  a CRNA program 2 years’ experience in a faculty leadership position in a CRNA program A record of scholarship and extramural funding · Required Skills: A strong and demonstrated commitment to integrating the clinical mission of the academy. Proven ability to provide leadership in a complex environment. Demonstrated leadership and effectiveness in building strong working relationships with a collaborative leadership style. Enjoys interacting with people and can easily connect with faculty and staff in the College and University across disciplines and among external entities in the community. Demonstrated experience working in a faculty, staff, and student environment as a faculty member. Evidence of successful collaborations with community partners and faculty teams in an academic setting; effective communication skills; knowledge of nursing academic curricula and programs; plans and conducts effective meetings; and evidence of leadership ability Demonstrated ability to be engaging and persuasive with strong teamwork skills, politically astute, diplomatic, and able to manage by influence. Flexible and capable of responding to multiple demands in a time-sensitive manner Ability to exercise astute judgment in all matters related to academic affairs To apply, please click on Interfolio link apply.interfolio.com/192626 and submit letter of intent, CV, and three professional references.  To inquire about the application process, please contact Nursing-HR@ouhsc.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191603": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Pharmacy Location: OU Health Center  TITLE: Adult Medicine Pharmacotherapy, Oklahoma City campus, faculty appointment as Clinical Assistant Professor (Full-time, limited term, non-tenure track) FUNCTIONS: The individual in this position reports to the Chair, Department of Pharmacy: Clinical and Administrative Sciences and is expected to support the tripartite mission of teaching, service and research/scholarly activity. This position will support comprehensive adult medicine pharmacotherapy services in Oklahoma City. Applicants are expected to develop scholarship in the area of adult medicine or medicine subspecialties, participate in collaborative research, and to develop and provide didactic, laboratory, and experiential training and education to doctor of pharmacy students and pharmacy practice and specialty residents. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: 1. Doctor of Pharmacy degree from an ACPE-accredited school or college of pharmacy 2. A valid and unrestricted license to practice pharmacy in Oklahoma and an Oklahoma preceptor license. 3. PGY1 plus PGY2 residency in internal medicine or medicine subspecialty area, two-year pharmacotherapy residency, or equivalent clinical experience with significant exposure to adult medicine. DISTINCTIVE CHARACTERISTICS: Excellent written, verbal, and computer skills; a strong working knowledge of pharmacy practice, as well as state and federal pharmacy laws, rules and regulations; and the ability to interact with pharmacists and healthcare team members in acute care practice settings are required. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: 1. Board certification in respective practice area(s) 2. Experience in classroom teaching, small group discussions, and precepting doctor of pharmacy students. 3. Post-graduate degree(s) in applicable area REPRESENTATIVE DUTIES: 1. (40%) Clinical Pharmacy Services. Provide direct patient care and support to the inpatient internal medicine service at the assigned site(s). Collaborate with other care providers to assure optimal pharmacotherapy outcomes for patients receiving treatment at the assigned site(s). Provide education for patients and health care providers at the assigned site(s). Measure and document the impact of the service on the quality and cost of care to the patient at the assigned site(s). 2. (30%) Teaching. Provide experiential training for doctor of pharmacy students at all levels in the curriculum as assigned. Serve as a preceptor for ASHP-accredited pharmacy residency programs including learners in the postgraduate year one (PGY1) and postgraduate year two (PGY2) programs and support these programs through development and recruitment activities. Support the professional program through didactic lectures, active learning strategies, participation in laboratory skills-based training, and/or course coordination to students at all stages of the program as assigned. 3. (20%) Scholarship. Disseminate new knowledge through publication of peer-reviewed abstracts and manuscripts, leading to production of peer-reviewed publications. Collaborate in research and/or scholarly activity with other College of Pharmacy faculty and/or College of Medicine faculty and/or affiliated pharmacy staff. 4. (10%) University and College service. Serve on professional and/or academic committees in the college or community as assigned by the Dean and Department Chair. Participate in regional, national, or international professional pharmacy or other health care associations. Other service activity that supports the college mission, academic or research community. Individuals interested in applying should upload the following materials (in pdf format) to Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/191603 : 1) a cover letter describing your interest and alignment with the position, 2) CV, statements on your 3) research interest and 4) teaching portfolio (one page each), and 5) the names and contact information of three references who would be willing to write letters of recommendation on your behalf. For questions or assistance email Jeana Sandoval (Jeana-sandoval@ou.edu). Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188180": {
      "title": "Communication Sciences and Disorders - Clinical Assistant Professor - Limited Term - Speech-Language Pathology",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Allied Health: Communication Sciences & Disorders Location: Oklahoma City, OK Direct Supervisor: Department Chair and Keys Clinic Director FTE: 100% Appointment Type: Limited-Term Title/Rank: Clinical Assistant Professor Primary Location: OU Health Center - Oklahoma City, OK Primary Responsibilities Job duties include: Clinical supervision of student interns in the Master of Arts in Speech-Language Pathology program Continuous direct patient care within the John W. Keys Speech and Hearing Center Instruction of didactic coursework to undergraduate and professional students Participation in the academic missions of the department, college, and university. This is primarily a clinical position with service and teaching responsibilities appropriate to the applicant’s experience and expertise. Required: Applicants must hold the Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-language Pathology (CCC-SLP) and have completed at least one year of successful work experience after earning the CCC-SLP. In addition, applicants must have completed at least two (2) hours of professional development in clinical instruction/supervision. Applicants should possess excellent communication, team building, problem-solving, and leadership skills. Preferred: Preferred qualifications include experience with pediatric diagnostics and treatment, and previous supervision experience. Applications should include a cover letter describing qualifications and experience, a complete curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for three references. Applicants should apply at: apply.interfolio.com/188180 If you have questions or issues when applying, please contact Deborah Martin at deborah-martin@ou.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175251": {
      "title": "Sr. Research -  Rehabilitation Department -  Associate/Full Professor  -Tenure Eligible",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Allied Health: Rehabilitation Sciences Location: Oklahoma City Direct Supervisor: Department Chair FTE: 1.0 Appointment Type: Tenure-Eligible Title and Rank: Associate/Full Professor Position Overview: Primary responsibilities include serving as the Director of the PhD program in Rehabilitation Sciences (RS), chairing and serving on dissertation committees, graduate course instruction, junior faculty and graduate student mentoring, and maintaining an extramurally funded research program. The successful candidate will devote approximately 70% effort to research, with expectations to develop and sustain an externally funded research program aligned with the Department’s mission and NIH or equivalent funding priorities. Position will contribute to the strategic growth of RS research within OU Health’s integrated academic medical system and advance the RS PhD program through leadership, mentoring, and development of externally funded collaborative research Research/Scholarship: Maintain an organized, viable, and funded research program using internal and external collaborations and resources. Maintain a consistent record of research dissemination activities to include publications and presentations through local, national, and international opportunities. Mentor professional and post-professional students, junior faculty in research activities Required Qualifications: PhD in rehabilitation science or a related discipline (e.g., physical therapy, occupational therapy, gerontology, nursing, movement science, kinesiology, neuroscience, public health, or other fields relevant to rehabilitation). Current experience as Principal Investigator on grants Teaching experience in graduate programs Evidence of successful mentoring of PhD students, MS students, and/or post-doctoral scholars. Experience in course and curriculum design. Records of Service in professional associations Eligible for Level 4 authority in the OUHC Graduate Faculty Appointment https://graduate.ouhsc.edu/Information-For/Faculty-Staff/Apply-to-be-a-Faculty-Member#1003916009-view-guidelines-as-a-pdf Preferred Qualifications: Experience in program development or administration, such as directing graduate programs or leading curriculum initiatives. Current or recently funded by NIH R01 or equivalent mechanism. Experience in interdisciplinary collaboration Applications should include a cover letter describing qualifications and experience, a complete curriculum vitae, a 2-3 page research statement, and contact information for references. If you have questions or issues when applying, please contact Lauren-Gavin at lauren-gavin@ou.edu"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175254": {
      "title": "Researcher - Associate Professor or Assistant Professor - Rehabilitation Sciences - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Allied Health: Rehabilitation Sciences Location: Oklahoma City, OK Direct Supervisor: Department Chair FTE: 100 % Appointment Type: Tenure-track Title/Rank: Associate Professor or Assistant Professor Primary Location: OU Health Campus in Oklahoma City, OK Primary Responsibilities: Include research and teaching in the Rehabilitation Sciences (RS) Department, including chairing and serving on dissertation committees, graduate course instruction, mentorship to professional, graduate, and post-professional students, and conducting extramurally funded research. The successful candidate will devote approximately 70% effort to research, with expectations to develop and sustain an externally funded research program aligned with the Department’s mission and NIH or equivalent funding priorities. Position will contribute to the strategic growth of RS research within OU Health’s integrated academic medical system and advance the RS PhD program through leadership, mentoring, and development of externally funded collaborative research. Research/Scholarship: Establish an organized, viable, and funded research agenda using internal and external collaborations and resources. Maintain a consistent record of research dissemination activities to include publications and presentations through local, national, and international opportunities. Mentor professional and post-professional students in research activities. JOB REQUIREMENTS Required PhD in rehabilitation science or a related discipline (e.g., physical therapy, occupational therapy, gerontology, nursing, movement science, kinesiology, neuroscience, public health, or other fields relevant to rehabilitation). Experience in grant writing and management Teaching experience in higher education Publication records in related fields Eligible for Level 4 authority in the OUHC Graduate Faculty Appointment https://graduate.ouhsc.edu/Information-For/Faculty-Staff/Apply-to-be-a-Faculty-Member#1003916009-view-guidelines-as-a-pdf Preferences (Not Required) Experience with teaching in graduate programs. Evidence of successful mentoring of PhD students, MS students Experience with course and curriculum design. Experience in interdisciplinary collaboration Applicants are required to provide an updated CV, a Cover Letter, a Research Statement, and contact information for references . For additional information, please email Lauren Gavin at lauren-gavin@ou.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176432": {
      "title": "Researcher - Associate Professor or Assistant Professor - Rehabilitation Sciences - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Allied Health: Rehabilitation Sciences Location: Oklahoma City, OK Direct Supervisor: Department Chair FTE: 100 % Appointment Type: Tenure-track Title/Rank: Associate Professor or Assistant Professor Primary Location: OU Health Campus in Oklahoma City, OK Primary Responsibilities: Include research and teaching in the Rehabilitation Sciences (RS) Department, including chairing and serving on dissertation committees, graduate course instruction, mentorship to professional, graduate, and post-professional students, and conducting extramurally funded research. The successful candidate will devote approximately 70% effort to research, with expectations to develop and sustain an externally funded research program aligned with the Department’s mission and NIH or equivalent funding priorities. Position will contribute to the strategic growth of RS research within OU Health’s integrated academic medical system and advance the RS PhD program through leadership, mentoring, and development of externally funded collaborative research. Research/Scholarship: Establish an organized, viable, and funded research agenda using internal and external collaborations and resources. Maintain a consistent record of research dissemination activities to include publications and presentations through local, national, and international opportunities. Mentor professional and post-professional students in research activities. JOB REQUIREMENTS Required PhD in rehabilitation science or a related discipline (e.g., physical therapy, occupational therapy, gerontology, nursing, movement science, kinesiology, neuroscience, public health, or other fields relevant to rehabilitation). Experience in grant writing and management Teaching experience in higher education Publication records in related fields Eligible for Level 4 authority in the OUHC Graduate Faculty Appointment https://graduate.ouhsc.edu/Information-For/Faculty-Staff/Apply-to-be-a-Faculty-Member#1003916009-view-guidelines-as-a-pdf Preferences (Not Required) Experience with teaching in graduate programs. Evidence of successful mentoring of PhD students, MS students Experience with course and curriculum design. Experience in interdisciplinary collaboration Applicants are required to provide an updated CV, a Cover Letter, a Research Statement, and contact information for references . For additional information, please email Lauren Gavin at lauren-gavin@ou.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/152478": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Prosthodontics",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Dentistry: Restorative Sciences Location: OUHSC - College of Dentistry  The University of Oklahoma College of Dentistry is seeking a Full-time Clinical Assistant/Associate/Professor in the Department of Restorative Sciences, Division of Prosthodontics.  Primary responsibilities include didactic, pre-clinical, and clinical courses in Fixed, Removable and Implant dentistry for our undergraduate dental program.  Intramural faculty practice, and research are encouraged.  Faculty are expected to be actively involved with University committees, continuing education and outreach, along with other tasks assigned by the Division Head. Successful applicants will join a team committed to quality educational programs and a broad spectrum of clinical care.  The OU College of Dentistry has recently committed to digital dentistry integration. The successful candidate will play a vital role in this effort. Oklahoma is a family friendly and inviting area. Oklahoma City is continually growing and provides the benefits of a large metropolitan area. Candidates must have a DDS/DMD from a CODA accredited dental school or foreign equivalent and completion of Part I and Part II of National Dental Board Examinations.  Master’s degree or Certificate in Prosthodontics from a CODA accredited dental school is preferred.  Salary and rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Evaluations of applicants will be begin immediately with the anticipation of the successful candidate to start Fall 2024.  Applications will be reviewed as received. Please submit your application in Interfolio to include: Curriculum vitae (CV) Letter of interest/cover letter 3 letters of reference"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179396": {
      "title": "Division Head of Prosthodontics, Assistant/Associate/Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Dentistry: Restorative Sciences Location: OUHSC The University of Oklahoma College of Dentistry Restorative Sciences Department is seeking a(n) Assistant/Associate/Professor and Division Head of Prosthodontics. RESPONSIBILITIES The Division Head of Prosthodontics provides leadership and administrative oversight for all divisional operations, including academic and clinical activities. The Division Head ensures alignment with the mission of the University of Oklahoma College of Dentistry and compliance with CODA accreditation standards. This role fosters excellence in education, patient care, and service while promoting innovation, interprofessional collaboration, and professional development within the college and beyond. The Division Head provides administrative and leadership oversight for divisional operations across prosthodontic educational and clinical programs, including pre-doctoral fixed, removable, and implantology. Responsibilities include developing and managing divisional budgets; recruiting, mentoring, managing and evaluating faculty and staff; and ensuring compliance with accreditation standards and university policies. The Division Head leads regular division meetings and conducts program meetings as appropriate. Additional responsibilities include overseeing faculty calibration activities, monitoring course director reporting on student performance, and serving on college and university committees as assigned. The Division Head leads divisional strategic planning to ensure alignment with the college’s mission and represents the division in college-wide and university-level initiatives, serving as a key advocate for prosthodontic education and clinical care. The Division Head is responsible for the development, delivery, and continuous improvement of preclinical and clinical prosthodontic curriculum, ensuring curricular integrity and educational excellence. Duties include monitoring student didactic and clinical progress, coordinating teaching assignments, appointing and supporting course directors, delivering didactic instruction, and providing clinical supervision. Proficiency with academic and administrative platforms such as Canvas, Simple Syllabus, and Microsoft Excel is required to effectively manage these responsibilities. The Division Head ensures the highest standards of patient care within prosthodontic clinical teaching environments and integrates evidence-based practices throughout clinical instruction. Proficiency with Axium is required, including collaboration with various teams within the college to support clinical operations, reporting, and assessment of student progress. EDUCATION: DDS or DMD from a CODA accredited institution or foreign equivalent and completion of Part I and Part II of National Dental Board Examinations. Preferred: Completion of a CODA-accredited Prosthodontics residency program with a certificate in Prosthodontics or Master's degree in Prosthodontics. EXPERIENCE: Minimum of three (3) years of clinical practice experience. Demonstrated leadership experience in academic, clinical, or administrative settings. LICENSES & CERTIFICATIONS: Must be eligible for licensure in the State of Oklahoma. Employment is contingent upon obtaining an Oklahoma dental license. Evaluations of applicants will begin immediately and will be reviewed as received. Please submit your application in Interfolio to include: Curriculum vitae (CV) Letter of interest/cover letter 3 letters of reference For consideration, please review the posted position requirements and apply now. For any questions or issues while applying please contact: Kayla Harp - Human Resources (kayla-harp@ou.edu or (405)271-5444)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182978": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Operative Dentistry",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Dentistry: Restorative Sciences Location: OUHSC The University of Oklahoma College of Dentistry is seeking a full-time Assistant Professor in the Department of Restorative Sciences, Division of Operative Dentistry. This position will report to the Division Head of Operative Dentistry and primary responsibilities include teaching didactic and pre-clinical courses. This includes the development and organization of course materials, schedules, handouts, syllabi, and teaching aids. In addition to the courses, other duties include supervision of pre-doctoral students in clinic relating to Operative Dentistry for our undergraduate dental program.  Intramural faculty practice, and research are encouraged.  Faculty are expected to be actively involved with University committees, continuing education and outreach, along with other tasks assigned by the Division Head. Successful applicants will join a team committed to quality educational programs and a broad spectrum of clinical care.  Oklahoma is a family friendly and inviting area. Oklahoma City is continually growing and provides the benefits of a large metropolitan area. Candidates must have a DDS/DMD from a CODA accredited dental school or foreign equivalent and completion of Part I and Part II of National Dental Board Examinations.    Salary and rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Evaluations of applicants will be begin immediately with the anticipation of the successful candidate to start in 2026. Applications will be reviewed as received. Please submit your application in Interfolio to include: Curriculum vitae (CV) Letter of interest/cover letter 3 letters of reference For questions, please reach out to Kayla Harp at Kayla-Harp@ou.edu ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/158695": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery Head and Neck Oncologist",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Dentistry: Surgical Sciences Location: Oklahoma City, OK Direct Supervisor:  Department Chair FTE: 50% Appointment Type: Limited Term Title/Rank: Clinical Assistant Professor Primary Location: OU Health Sciences Center - Oklahoma City, OK The Division of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery at the University of Oklahoma College of Dentistry seeks qualified applicants for a part-time Clinical Assistant Professor to join our Cleft and Craniofacial Team. The position will be responsible for all academic, patient care, research, and administrative functions of the program consistent with applicable rules, regulations, or guidelines of the College of Dentistry, the University of Oklahoma and the American Dental Association Council on Accreditation. The successful candidate will join an the surgical sciences department committed to excellence in teaching didactic and clinical courses in the post-doctoral oral and maxillofacial surgery program.  Responsibilities will include: Developing, implementing, and supervising a quality post-doctoral education program for Residents at the College of Dentistry. Assigning and scheduling faculty to specific teaching responsibilities in a way that will maximize the quality of the pre-doctoral educational program. Preparing course schedules for each semester. Participating in research and encouraging research by pre-doctoral students and residents Participating at periodic meetings of the program faculty; performing other duties necessary for effective and efficient operation of the oral and maxillofacial surgery pre-doctoral educational program. Diagnosis of pathological or irregular oral conditions Administering local anesthesia Performing admissions, work-up, and performance of surgical procedures of patients with illnesses, injuries, and disorders of both the functional and aesthetic aspects of the hard and soft tissues of the oral and maxillofacial regions. Performing dental-alveolar surgical procedures, placement of dental implants and biopsy procedures, and ambulatory OMS procedures. Performing routine and complex extraction of teeth, exostosis removal and routine pre-prosthetic surgeries. Education and supervision of Oral Maxillofacial Surgery residents, dental residents, interns, and dental students. DDS/DMD from CODA accredited dental school or foreign equivalent and completion of Part I and Part II of National Board Examinations. Certificate in Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery from CODA accredited residency program or foreign equivalent training. Experience in dental education and experience with electronic medical records preferred. Eligibility for Oklahoma specialty dental licensure/faculty teaching permit required. Cleft and Craniofacial Specialty Preferred. Interested applicants should upload a copy of their CV/Resume, Cover letter and 3 letters of reference within Interfolio. For any questions about the position, please contact Dr. Paul Tiwana, Department Chair & Division Head at paul-tiwana@ouhsc.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/178461": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Medicine: Biochemistry & Physiology Location: Oklahoma City, OK Seeking a full time Associate Professor, tenure track faculty member in the area of metabolic pathophysiology. The faculty member will join a vibrant group of investigators in the role of metabolic reprogramming in diabetes, obesity, diabetic complications and aging, and geroscience. This position provides a unique opportunity to interact and collaborate with leading scientists in the Harold Hamm Diabetes Center, the Nathan Shock Center on Aging, the Dean McGee Eye Institute, and the Stephenson Cancer Center on the OUHC campus and the Oklahoma Medical Research Foundation and Oklahoma City VA Medical Center located next to the OUHC campus. Job requirements include evidence of outstanding research productivity and a PhD, MD or equivalent. Candidates should submit a curriculum vitae, a description of current research interests and future research plans. Please contact Ginnia Smith with any questions or issues; email ginnia-smith@ou.edu or 405-271-8001 ext. 56244."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189954": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Cell Biology 00091453",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Medicine: Cell Biology Location: Oklahoma City The Department of Cell Biology at the University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Campus (OUHC) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in any area of cell biology. Applicants will be considered at the assistant, associate, or professor stage. Areas of particular interest include neuroscience, in particular focus on cellular and molecular mechanisms, and developmental biology but all areas of cell biology will be considered. The successful candidates are expected to maintain independent and dynamic extramurally funded research programs. The Department of Cell Biology is one of five basic science departments within the College of Medicine at OUHC, providing a highly interactive cohort of scientists with interests in neuroscience, cilia, cell signaling, vision, cardiovascular biology and cancer. The department houses a state-of the-art imaging center which includes two super-resolution microscopes that are capable of 3D-SIM, STORM and optical reassignment based live-cell super-resolution imaging, two-photon and confocal microscopy, as well as long-duration live cell epifluorescence imaging and a full-service histology core. For further information about the department go to https://basicsciences.ouhsc.edu/cb/. Faculty members in the Cell Biology Department have the opportunity to mentor competitive graduate students through a variety of doctoral programs offered on the OUHC campus, including Cell Biology and Neuroscience. OUHC is a comprehensive health center that includes Colleges of Pharmacy, Dentistry, Nursing, Allied Health, Public Health, Medicine, and the Graduate College. It is home to two hospitals and an NCI-designated Cancer Center. OUHC Core Facilities include the state-of-the-art Laboratory for Molecular Biology and Cytometry Research, which provides services specializing in genomics, proteomics, bioinformatics, cytometry, and imaging. The Oklahoma Medical Research Foundation (OMRF) is adjacent to OUHC and maintains a collaborative partnership with OUHC. Scientists at OMRF are also a source of collaborators for studies in this field. OMRF core facilities are available to OUHC investigators. OUHC is located in downtown Oklahoma City, the country’s 20th largest city. The greater Oklahoma City area has a rich cultural base with modern, vibrant business and entertainment districts. The cost of living is enviably low relative to other university communities across the country. Successful applicants will receive a competitive salary, Job requirements include evidence of an established outstanding federally funded research program and a PhD, MD or equivalent. Candidates should submit a curriculum vitae, a description of current research interests and future research plans. Letters of recommendation will be requested at a later stage. The deadline to receive materials is October 15, 2026."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/185951": {
      "title": "Gastroenterology Faculty, Assistant/Associate/Professor in Research",
      "description": "Department: University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center: Provost Office: College of Medicine: Internal Medicine Location: Oklahoma City Academic Appointment Full-time faculty position with appointment at the level of Assistant/Associate/Professor in the Department of Medicine, College of Medicine, University of Oklahoma Health Campus.  This position is open rank with the Clinician Scientist pathway, appointment will be consecutive term. Areas of Responsibilities Designing and conducting studies (clinical trials, translational, or outcomes research) Publishing in peer-reviewed journals Applying for and managing grants (e.g., NIH funding) Leading or collaborating on multidisciplinary research teams Turning lab discoveries into treatments Maintain and manage a research laboratory through grant funding Required Qualifications: Doctoral Degree (PhD, MD, or equivalent) MD candidates must be either Board Eligible or Board Certified by the American Board of Internal Medicine Strong research training Strong communication skills Ethical conduct in research Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of potential for independent funding History of securing grants/ability to obtain external funding National/International reputation To apply, please provide a CV at apply.interfolio.com/185951 Please send any questions to intmedchair@ou.edu."
    },
